 ],
 "notes": "Associations are matched per subnet (assoc refs subnet); that the three associations of a tier share one route table, and that each NAT uses its own EIP, are not expressible (ref has no per-instance binding), so nats_use_eips and the association checks are partial. Gateway ids in routes are unknown at plan, so routes to the IGW/NAT are ref checks; app_nat_routes_per_zone counts the default routes (inline tables >=4, or >=3 separate aws_route; a mixed inline-public plus separate-private encoding with only two private routes would wrongly pass). The explicit local route is not checked on its own: real templates rely on the implicit local route, so the database table is checked for having no inline 0.0.0.0/0 route; a default route added to it as a separate aws_route resource is not detectable (exists cannot express 'at most N' with zero allowed), so that check is partial. env_prefixes_name_tags accepts var.env or a local named *prefix/*env, since two of three real templates build the prefix in a local. Reviewed 2026-11-11 against 3 real templates: all pass all core."
}